{% extends 'legal/_layout.html.twig' %}

{% block title %}Cookie notice{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
    <p>
        We use <strong>no tracking, analytics or advertising cookies</strong>. You can browse the statistics and reports
        without a single cookie being set. That's why there is no cookie banner.
    </p>

    <h2>Which cookies do we set?</h2>
    <p>Only when you submit a report do we set two functional cookies that the form needs to work:</p>
    <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Retention</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr>
                <td><code>__Host-csrf-token_…</code></td>
                <td>Security: stops another website from submitting a report on your behalf (CSRF protection).</td>
                <td>Until you close your browser</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><code>PHPSESSID</code></td>
                <td>Session: shows the "Thank you for your report" confirmation after submitting.</td>
                <td>Until you close your browser</td>
            </tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>
        These cookies are strictly necessary for a service you ask for, so no consent is required (Dutch
        Telecommunications Act, article 11.7a, implementing the EU ePrivacy Directive). They contain no plate or other
        report data. We also don't use <code>localStorage</code> or similar browser storage.
    </p>

    <p>
        Moderators who log in to the admin area also get a session cookie (<code>PHPSESSID</code>) to stay logged in.
        Visitors and reporters only get it as described above.
    </p>

    <h2>Appearance</h2>
    <p>
        If you pick an appearance (light or dark) at the top of the site, we remember that choice in the cookie
        <code>theme</code> for one year. Pick "System" again and we remove it, and the site follows your device. The
        cookie only holds that choice.
    </p>

    <h2>OpenStreetMap maps</h2>
    <p>
        Your browser loads the maps from OpenStreetMap's servers, which therefore receive your IP address. As far as we
        know, OpenStreetMap sets no cookies through these map tiles. See the
        <a href="https://osmfoundation.org/wiki/Privacy_Policy" rel="noopener">OSMF privacy policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Deleting cookies</h2>
    <p>
        You can delete or block cookies at any time in your browser settings. If you block the functional cookies, you
        can't submit a report, but browsing still works.
    </p>

    <p>Read more about how we handle data in our <a href="{{ path('legal', {page: 'privacy'}) }}">privacy statement</a>.</p>
{% endblock %}
